{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]I been hangin' [Ab]out of town lord in that [Cm]low down [Bb]rain[Eb]
[Eb]Watchin' good time Charlie friend [Ab]is drivin' me insane[Cm][Bb][Eb][Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Up on shady Charlotte [Ab]Street lord the green lights look red[Cm][Bb][Eb]
[Eb]Wish I was back home [Ab]on the farm lord [Cm]in my [Bb]feather [Eb]bed.[Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
And I [Eb]got [Ab]myself a rockin' [Cm]chair, to [Bb]see if I can [Eb]lose
These [Ab]thin, [Bb]dime [Cm]hard [Bb]times, [Ab]hell on [Bb]Church Street [Eb]blues.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Found myself a picker friend who's read yesterday's news
Folded up page twenty-one and stuck it in my shoe
Gave me a nickle to the poor my good turn for the day
Folded up my own bill fold threw it far away.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I wish I had some guitar strings Old Black Diamond brand
I'd string up this old Martin box and go and join some band
But I guess I'm gonna stay right here and pick and sing a while
Try to make me a little change and give them folks a smile.
{end_of_chorus}

